# What never belongs in the build context.
#
# node_modules alone is hundreds of megabytes of the wrong platform's binaries
# — the image builds its own with `npm ci`. Sending it makes every build slow
# and can poison it with host-built native modules.

.git
.github
.claude

**/node_modules
library-frontend/dist
school-library-system/uploads
school-library-system/school-library-system
school-library-system/school-library-system.exe

# Secrets never go into an image layer. compose passes .env at run time.
.env
*.env
!.env.example

# Docs, tooling and scratch — none of it is needed to build.
*.md
tools/
deploy/
demo-snapshot/
"Hedef Kutuphane clickable prototype (1)"
